This product includes modified Python/NumPy/numba adaptations of portions of
ppf-contact-solver, including closest-feature distance, additive continuous
collision detection, and LBVH structure/query concepts. ppf-contact-solver is
available at https://github.com/st-tech/ppf-contact-solver and is licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

For a reproducible upstream source snapshot corresponding to these adaptations,
see ppf-contact-solver commit
8b7740b032131aeeb46f51d882c96e09b171acc8. Retained records do not establish
that this was the exact historical checkout, so CoupFE does not make that
stronger claim.

    Copyright 2025 Ryoichi Ando (ZOZO, Inc.)

CoupFE's adaptations are identified in coupfe/operators/contact.py,
coupfe/operators/contact3d.py, coupfe/operators/contact3d_numba.py, and
coupfe/operators/bvh_numba.py.

The research examples `phasefield_corrosion_cui`, `gel_chester_anand`,
`stabilized_tet4`, and `morphing_hex8`, together with the code-generation
proofs `neo_hookean_umat`, `ogden_umat`, `small_strain_j2_umat`, and
`small_strain_viscoelastic_umat`, contain project-authored source ported from
abaqus_ufl commit
0f525339db1aad70e9f8f4825a02c1164f0da7a0. Those example sources were
published under the MIT License, Copyright 2026 Teng Zhang; see
LICENSE-ABAQUS-UFL-EXAMPLES. The pinned source and its CREDITS record
distinguish project source from formulation, benchmark, mesh, and solver-data
lineage:
https://github.com/tengzhang48/abaqus_ufl/tree/0f525339db1aad70e9f8f4825a02c1164f0da7a0

